menu "SD stream server"

config APP_UI_FIT_CHECK
    bool "Run the UI memory fit check at startup"
    default y
    help
        Creates a throwaway LVGL screen once the services are running, reports what
        its memory cost and where it came from, then frees it. It exists to prove
        that the interface's memory is external by construction and that internal
        RAM is untouched - the margin Wi-Fi needs for its contiguous DMA buffers.
        When the real interface replaces main/ui_fit.c, this option goes with it.

        See docs/research/radio-player-memory-and-lvgl.md.

endmenu
